{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2456","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2456","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2456\",\"parent_revision\":\"73f9275af17284f3e9f83127b50405d2099b2670\",\"root_revision\":\"72934c8ea103b5126487be524aeddc787005e3ab7290b2c2064c90dbdd51d3b2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen `complete-implementation` creates a quality gate plan, the orchestrator constructs a 7-task array containing all field values \u2014 task titles, agent assignments, dependency chains, priority values \u2014 and passes the entire schema to `sam_plan(action='create', tasks=[...])`. The `complete-implementation` skill references `build_quality_gate_plan(slug, issue, impl_plan_address)` as the intended generation step, but when the `sam_plan` MCP tool schema was loaded via ToolSearch, the `create` action accepted a `tasks` array (not `tasks_yaml`), and no `build_quality_gate_plan` function appeared as a callable MCP tool. The orchestrator constructed the 7-task array manually from the phase table in the skill.\\n\\nThe SAM server owns the quality gate phase mapping (T0\u2013T6, standard agents, standard dependency chain). The orchestrator passes three parameters \u2014 slug, issue, impl_plan_address \u2014 that fully determine the standard QG task set. Despite this, the data passes across the boundary from the orchestrator to the server rather than the server generating the standard plan internally from the three inputs.\\n\\nObserved: `complete-implementation` session 2026-05-25, QG plan P49573878, issue #2437. Affected: every `complete-implementation` run that creates a quality gate plan.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|-------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description + `sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lines 379\u2013396, `quality_gates.py` |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `sam_schema/server.py` (`@mcp.tool` pattern), `quality_gates.build_quality_gate_plan` |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | Existing tests in `tests/test_quality_gates.py` |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | Full source readable; server and quality_gates modules confirmed |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | TDD path clear; existing test file extends naturally |\\n\\n**Gap (design decision \u2014 not a planning blocker):** The correct MCP interface shape is undecided \u2014 new `action='create_quality_gates'` variant on `sam_plan`, or a standalone `sam_create_quality_gate_plan` tool. This choice affects only the server implementation and the SKILL.md call site; it does not affect task decomposition.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **complete-implementation qg plan creation requires orchestrators to construct and transmit the full task schema to sam_plan** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-05-25 \u2014 complete-implementation run for issue #2437\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Blocks**: Every `complete-implementation` run that creates a full QG plan (every SAM-path feature). Each run sends a 7-task schema payload over the MCP boundary instead of 3 parameters.\\n- **Drift risk**: The inline task array in SKILL.md and `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` in `quality_gates.py` can diverge silently. No tests prevent a SKILL.md-only phase change from going undetected.\\n- **Blast radius**: `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (call site), `sam_schema/server.py` (new tool), `sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` (existing logic, unchanged), `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` and `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` (already reference the intended design).\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Orchestrators pass 3 parameters (slug, issue, impl_plan_address) instead of constructing and transmitting a 7-field task array.\\n- The QG phase mapping becomes a single source of truth in `quality_gates.py` \u2014 changes are automatically reflected in all future runs without updating SKILL.md.\\n- The inline task array in SKILL.md lines 379-396 can be replaced with a single MCP call, reducing SKILL.md complexity.\\n- The existing `tests/test_quality_gates.py` already covers `build_quality_gate_plan` correctness; adding a server-side wrapper adds thin MCP boundary coverage only.\\n- Aligns runtime behavior with the architectural documentation: `backlog-item-lifecycle.md` line 610 and `workflow-architecture-diagram.md` line 79 already describe `build_quality_gate_plan()` as the actor at the `P6_QG_BUILD` node.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` exposes a callable that accepts `(slug, issue, impl_plan_address)` and returns a QG plan address without requiring the orchestrator to construct the task array.\\n- `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` Quality Gate Plan Creation Step 2 references the new MCP entry point instead of the inline task array.\\n- `tests/test_quality_gates.py` or a new test file covers the MCP tool boundary.\\n- `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` and `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` remain consistent with the new call site (they already describe the intended design).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. A `fastmcp call` against the SAM server with `slug`, `issue`, and `impl_plan_address` as the only inputs creates a QG plan containing exactly 7 tasks matching `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` order and returns a plan address.\\n2. `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` Quality Gate Plan Creation Step 2 no longer contains an inline task array \u2014 it references the MCP tool with the 3-parameter signature.\\n3. The inline 7-task `tasks=[...]` literal in SKILL.md lines 379-396 is removed.\\n4. Running `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gates.py` (and any new server-side tests) exits 0.\\n5. `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` node `P6_QG_BUILD` description matches the new MCP call site.\\n6. No second copy of the QG phase definitions exists outside `sam_schema/core/quality_gates._PHASE_DEFINITIONS`.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 `build_quality_gate_plan()`, `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `@mcp.tool` registration pattern |\\n| Source | `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lines 379-396 \u2014 inline task array to be replaced |\\n| Test | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gates.py` \u2014 existing coverage of `build_quality_gate_plan` |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` line 610 \u2014 `P6_QG_BUILD` node contract |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` line 79 \u2014 `build_quality_gate_plan` already shown as the QG creation actor |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 `build_quality_gate_plan` is already implemented and tested.\\n- Blocks: None currently. Future QG phase changes will benefit from a single source of truth once this is resolved.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the Python function already exists and is tested. The work is: (1) add an MCP tool wrapper in `server.py` (~20-30 lines), (2) update `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` Step 2 to call the new tool instead of the inline array, (3) add MCP boundary test coverage, (4) update docs if needed. No new logic is introduced.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type: Refactor** \u2014 The quality-gate task schema already exists in `sam_schema/core/quality_gates._PHASE_DEFINITIONS` and `build_quality_gate_plan()` is already a tested Python function. The gap is that this logic was never wired into the MCP boundary. The orchestrator compensates by inlining the task array manually, duplicating the canonical source.\\n\\n**Root cause category: missing-guardrail** \u2014 No MCP tool enforces that the QG task schema is the server-side source of truth. The SKILL.md inline tasks array (lines 379-396) and `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` in `quality_gates.py` are now two independent copies of the same data. Any phase change must be applied in both places, and the SKILL.md copy is invisible to the test suite.\\n\",\"digest\":\"834cb8a5f2013636fa76d8b4dec024bf0d1517f68b4f75ca949b619e541038ec\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg2Twg\"}"}